    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11118" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏquīnus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		coquo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to cooking</i> (rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">forum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Ps. 3, 2, 1</span></i>
			 and 2.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏquīna</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A kitchen</i>, <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 37,
				4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Arn. 4, p. 130</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Non. p. 55,
			18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>The art of cooking, cookery</i>,
				<i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 2, p. 17, 4</span></i> (al.
			coquinaria).</div>
